* placeholder_devices.lib
* =============================================================================
*                    *** NOT A VENDOR MODEL LIBRARY ***
* =============================================================================
* DESIGN-TIME PLACEHOLDERS for the Fase 2 topology draft of the line
* preamplifier. AUTHORED BY HAND. Not derived from, not checked against, and
* not equivalent to any manufacturer model.
*
* Deliberately NOT placed in models/: models/ is the canonical, provenance-
* tracked library validated by scripts/validate_models.py (24/24). Adding
* unqualified placeholders there would corrupt that contract.
*
* WHY THESE EXIST AT ALL
* ----------------------
* The repo's stock generic models (models/bjt_npn/generic_npn.lib etc.) carry
* NO junction capacitances and NO transit time. A feedback amplifier built
* from them has no high-frequency poles at all, so a loop-gain simulation
* would report ~90 deg phase margin unconditionally - an answer that is worse
* than no answer, because it looks like evidence.
*
* These models add capacitances and transit times of PLAUSIBLE ORDER for the
* device classes chosen, so that the loop-gain / stability simulation produces
* a finite, falsifiable number. That number is a DESIGN-TIME SANITY CHECK, not
* a verified figure of merit.
*
* WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITH THEM
* -----------------------------
*  - Do NOT quote any THD / distortion figure obtained with these models.
*    Distortion is a property of the model's nonlinearity; these have generic
*    Gummel-Poon/Shichman-Hodges nonlinearity that was not fitted to anything.
*    Any THD number from this file is MEANINGLESS.
*  - Do NOT quote the phase margin as verified. It is provisional.
*  - Do NOT quote the noise figure as verified: KF/AF (flicker noise) are
*    zero here, so 1/f noise is entirely absent from any .noise run.
*
* REPLACE WITH, in Fase 3/4:
*  - LSK489 : transcribed by hand from the Linear Systems PDF, per the
*             mandatory procedure of ADR-013 (freeze PDF in vendor/ with
*             sha256, transcribe into models/jfet/, provenance must say
*             "transcribed manually from vendor PDF", cross-check IDSS/VP).
*  - THAT320: native .lib from THAT Corp (Fase 1 report: downloaded and
*             inspected - best SPICE provenance of the whole round).
*  - MJE15032/33, 2N5551, 2N5401: vendor models, provenance to be established
*             by bom-component-manager.
*
* Author: analog-topology-designer (Claude Opus 5), 2026-09-08,
*         on behalf of roberto.carmeli@gmail.com
* =============================================================================

* --- LSK489 half (N-channel JFET) ------------------------------------------
* Shichman-Hodges. VTO/BETA chosen to sit inside the LSK489 datasheet's own
* IDSS window (2.6-15 mA) at a mid grade: IDSS = BETA*VTO^2 = 2e-3*1.5^2
* = 4.5 mA.  CGD/CGS chosen so Ciss ~ 4 pF, the figure ADR-013 was decided on.
* LAMBDA is a guess. The cascode of ADR-014 is what makes that guess cheap.
.model LSK489X NJF (VTO=-1.5 BETA=2.0E-3 LAMBDA=0.010 IS=1E-14
+ RD=10 RS=10 CGS=2.9P CGD=1.1P PB=0.8 FC=0.5 KF=0 AF=1)

* --- 2N5551-class small-signal NPN (cascode, current sinks, Vbe multiplier)--
* fT ~ 300 MHz -> TF ~ 0.5 ns. BVceo 160 V in the real part; SPICE ignores it,
* so breakdown margin is a paper check, not a simulated one.
.model NSS2N5551 NPN (IS=1E-14 BF=150 VAF=100 IKF=0.15 NE=1.5 ISE=1E-13
+ BR=4 VAR=30 RB=20 RE=1 RC=5 CJE=12P VJE=0.7 MJE=0.33
+ CJC=4P VJC=0.5 MJC=0.33 TF=0.5N TR=50N XTB=1.5 KF=0 AF=1)

* --- 2N5401-class small-signal PNP (VAS) -----------------------------------
.model PSS2N5401 PNP (IS=1E-14 BF=120 VAF=80 IKF=0.10 NE=1.5 ISE=1E-13
+ BR=4 VAR=25 RB=20 RE=1 RC=5 CJE=15P VJE=0.7 MJE=0.33
+ CJC=6P VJC=0.5 MJC=0.33 TF=0.6N TR=50N XTB=1.5 KF=0 AF=1)

* --- THAT320-class matched monolithic PNP (input-stage current mirror) ------
* High beta, low VAF (small geometry), fT ~ 100 MHz.
.model PTHAT320 PNP (IS=1E-15 BF=200 VAF=60 IKF=0.05 NE=1.5 ISE=1E-14
+ BR=4 VAR=20 RB=40 RE=2 RC=10 CJE=10P VJE=0.7 MJE=0.33
+ CJC=3P VJC=0.5 MJC=0.33 TF=1.5N TR=50N XTB=1.5 KF=0 AF=1)

* --- MJE15032-class power NPN (output follower) ----------------------------
* fT 30 MHz *at high current*; at 15 mA it is much lower. TF=5.3n is the
* 30 MHz figure - i.e. OPTIMISTIC for the actual operating point. Cob ~ 100 pF.
.model NMJE15032 NPN (IS=1E-13 BF=100 VAF=100 IKF=1.0 NE=1.5 ISE=1E-12
+ BR=4 VAR=50 RB=5 RE=0.1 RC=0.5 CJE=300P VJE=0.7 MJE=0.33
+ CJC=100P VJC=0.5 MJC=0.4 TF=5.3N TR=500N XTB=1.5 KF=0 AF=1)

* --- MJE15033-class power PNP (output follower) ----------------------------
.model PMJE15033 PNP (IS=1E-13 BF=100 VAF=100 IKF=1.0 NE=1.5 ISE=1E-12
+ BR=4 VAR=50 RB=5 RE=0.1 RC=0.5 CJE=300P VJE=0.7 MJE=0.33
+ CJC=120P VJC=0.5 MJC=0.4 TF=6.4N TR=500N XTB=1.5 KF=0 AF=1)

* --- 1N4148-class small-signal diode (negative-rail bias reference) ---------
.model D1N4148 D (IS=2.5E-9 N=1.85 RS=0.6 CJO=2P VJ=0.7 M=0.33 TT=6N BV=100)
